{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/734872-homebrew-idea-new-type-of-family-dinner","id":734872,"title":"[Homebrew Idea] New Type Of Family Dinner","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-28T08:40:23-07:00","id":734872,"title":"[Homebrew Idea] New Type Of Family Dinner","content":"As written, Family Dinner allows a Beast to follow another supernatural creature on a hunt for metaphysical sustenance, thus gaining Satiety from it. But what if Beasts could generate a limited quantity of other splats' energies inside their Lair, and then invite said splats over by opening a Primordial Pathway to the Lair and offer protection from harmful Lair Traits?<br /> <br /> I am not sure what a good system would be like, but I'd say that the Beast needs ingredients, so to say. If he wants to generate Glamour, he gets goblin fruit. If he wants Mana, he gets Tass, and so on. The ST gets the final say on what counts as an ingredient, and may give bonuses due to impressive instances. I also don't know whether I should allow Beasts to generate more energy by destroying a more potent receptacle of energy, like a Token, Fetish, Artifact, etc. In any case, Aether cannot be generated with this permutation of Family Dinner, since Demons are not Kin. The Beast cannot cook a meal for a type of supernatural creature with whom he does not share the Family Ties Condition.<br /> <br /> The Beast spends 1 Satiety + 1 willpower, and rolls Intelligence + Occult + Lair. The target number of successes is equal to the number of Vitae/Essence/Mana etc he wants to generate x 2 (caps at Lair x 3). Each roll takes one hour. He may generate multiple types of energy. Dramatic Failure reduces the Beast to Satiety 0, but he can spend another willpower point make a Resolve + Composure roll to control the Horror and act as if he was at Satiety 1 for a number of scenes equal to his successes. Exceptional Success gives 1 willpower to all those to share the meal, and moves up the Impression of the Beast by one level for Social Maneuvering for one chapter. Lastly, this type of Family Dinner can only be done once per chapter.<br /> <br /> Another important thing is how the energy is given by the Lair. An Anakim might have luxurious swimming pools made of monstrous bones and filled with blood so good that a vampire only needs to bathe in it to feel strengthened. An Eshmaki's cornfield might have fungi, herbs and other foodstuffs filling clothes as if they were scarecrows.<br /> <br /> If this doesn't sound like a good idea for a template power, how about a Merit worth 3 to 5 dots? What if the amount of energy generated by the Lair was determined by how much Satiety was spent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-28-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:39:24-07:00","id":735167,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't... This be Both a Merit and Lair Traits?<br /> <br /> Merit: Feeding Grounds (3 or 5 Points)<br /> <br /> You may make your lair useful for others to feed within, with the 3 point version of this merit you may take 1 Lair Trait that provide Sustenance for other Types of supernaturals. You Must however understand them enough for you to Acquire Nightmares based upon their Supernatural Type. The Sustenance provided is fulfilling and bland, but is enough to sustain them.<br /> <br /> At 5 points you may take up to 3 Lair traits or may make 1 trait sufficiently Filling for the Supernatural Type of your Choice.<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Something like that? I'm Better at the Brainstorming then getting the ideas across.... but meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T11:40:31-07:00","id":735391,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea, but I'd make it more parallel to a beast's normal family feeding, ie the supernatural gets fed by vicariously feeding with the beast,<br /> <br /> And since this makes networking with other supernaturals really easy, I agree it's merit worthy. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T11:47:03-07:00","id":735427,"title":"","content":"Definitely wothwhile to consider, though it should have a predatorial component to it. I would tie it into the Children hunting dreams in the astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T22:57:12-08:00","id":787169,"title":"","content":"Been thinking about this for the last couple days and decided to try my hand at throwing something together.<br /> <br /> <b>Find a Vein (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Presence or Stamina rating of [Merit dots + 2]<br /> It is in the nature of the Begotten to feast, but the hungers of their kin tend to be more rarefied. A Beast with this Merit can provide for their family with a bit of effort, tapping into currents of stray supernatural energy that lie buried within the Primordial Dream called Veins.<br /> <br /> A Beast seeking to draw upon a Vein must first have room in their Lair to add a Chamber and possess the Family Ties Condition with a supernatural being capable of storing the energies they wish to draw forth. Having met these conditions, the Beast must satisfy their Hunger upon one or more similarly resonant supernatural beings with an act whose Satiety potential is 7 or higher in the presence of one or more of their Lair Traits and spend a point of Satiety as though adding a Chamber to the Lair; this confluence of metaphysical appetite is enough to bring forth a Vein of the appropriate supernatural energy in the Lair of the Beast and her brood.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the story, a pool of [dots in this Merit + Beast's Occult rating] points of an appropriate supernatural power currency runs through the Lair. This pool refreshes at the same rate as the Beast normally would lose Satiety over time (see p111) and can be refreshed at will with the expenditure of a dot of Satiety.<br /> <br /> This pool can be accessed from any Chamber in the Lair, but for every Burrow between a Chamber and the shortest route to the Beast's Heart, subtract one point from the pool of available power currency, to a minimum of zero; the last crumbs of the Begotten's meal must be scraped together from within the Heart itself. Supernatural beings with the Family Ties Condition tagged to the Beast mitigate this reduction of the pool by [Supernatural Tolerance/3 rounded up] points, though this does not increase the pool's maximum capacity; the bonds of Kinship permit the supernatural energies to flow more readily, but no amount of metaphysical closeness will change the amount of sustenance to be had. Any supernatural being that partakes of the feast subtracts one Door from Social Maneuvering attempts by the Beast to place the Family Ties Condition on them.<br /> <br /> Redefining the Burrows in a Lair with a Vein removes the Beast's Occult rating from the pool's maximum size until the next chapter. A Vein counts as a Chamber for the purposes of available slots in a given Beast's Lair, and tapping a Vein counts as adding a Chamber. At the end of the story, the Vein sinks back into the Dark Dream, though the Beast can prevent this from happening for the length of another story with the expenditure of a Willpower dot, which does not count as adding a Chamber to the Lair for the purposes of expanding the Lair but still fills an available Chamber slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T23:36:13-08:00","id":787176,"title":"","content":"This actually sounds pretty cool.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It does give a drawback in that you need to have vacant Chamber slots to tap a Vein, much less several. But then again, it's a temporary measure at best, and a way for capitalizing on Family Dinner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T17:59:16-08:00","id":790591,"title":"","content":"Nice work, Satchel! I'm impressed. My only nitpick is that I'd lower the Prerequisite to Stamina or Presence equal to the Merit's rating + 1.<br /> <br /> But how does the Vein manifest? Can I still have a blood fountain for vampires and a garden of twisted goblin fruit for changelings, for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T21:17:40-08:00","id":790667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/734872-homebrew-idea-new-type-of-family-dinner?p=790591#post790591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only nitpick is that I'd lower the Prerequisite to Stamina or Presence equal to the Merit's rating + 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly it's set up that way so that getting the back half of the Merit's potential dots requires raising Lair, but by all means adjust to taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But how does the Vein manifest? Can I still have a blood fountain for vampires and a garden of twisted goblin fruit for changelings, for example? </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking you're going to see something like a smaller-scale Hive Trait flavored by your Lair Traits, the aesthetics of the Heart, and the feeding that you engaged in to tap the Vein.<br /> <br /> For instance, if Dynamo sets about drawing up a Vein of Essence to fuel her cousin's fetish-crafting, the Jagged and Electrified substation that is her Heart threads tangles of cord from Chamber to Chamber. Occasionally the crackling of the exposed wires echoes the oath of vengeance sworn by the Jaggling who claimed the locus centered on the transformer that now sits in the Lair, but the Collector is understandably confident that the Halogen Princess will find her allies slower to act without the promise of sustenance.<br /> <br /> It's a broad enough concept, though as-written larger pools will by necessity have to account for the breadth of access in their presentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-22-2015, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T23:12:55-07:00","id":848631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/734872-homebrew-idea-new-type-of-family-dinner?p=787169#post787169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking about this for the last couple days and decided to try my hand at throwing something together.<br /> <br /> <b>Find a Vein (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Presence or Stamina rating of [Merit dots + 2]</div> </div> </div> </div>May I add this to my Homebrew Beast Merit thread, if it's alright?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T23:15:30-07:00","id":848633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/734872-homebrew-idea-new-type-of-family-dinner?p=848631#post848631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May I add this to my Homebrew Beast Merit thread, if it's alright?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go right ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}